[5] Comb-overlap Gram kernel bridge (mac-mini S75 integration)
K(p,q) := meas(D_p cap D_q) = <1_Dp, 1_Dq> is PSD by construction
S75 proved the single-arc row K(1,q)=1/(7q), q<=13:
K(1,1)=1/7, K(1,2)=1/14, K(1,3)=1/21, K(1,4)=1/28, K(1,5)=1/35, K(1,6)=1/42, K(1,7)=1/49, K(1,8)=1/56, K(1,9)=1/63, K(1,10)=1/70, K(1,11)=1/77, K(1,12)=1/84, K(1,13)=1/91
K(7,q) constant sidecar = 1/49
single-arc peeling: cap(P)=cap(P\{1})-(1/7)*(1-1/min(P\{1})) for speeds <=13
certificate use = finite spatial Gram basis dual to the Fejer Fourier kernel
remaining debt = order-3 triple-overlap constants, not the order-2 PSD kernel

