- Rejected vertices: runners, arcs, roots, q-coefficients, and famous constants alone.
- Chosen vertices: proof carriers, because the LRC predicate is certificate payload retention.
- Preserves: Fejer positivity/PSD, comb-Gram positivity, double-zero sharpness, cap-vs-sector split, conductor-7 labels.
- Destroys: literal runner identity, raw height/numerology, and any unlabelled scalar extremality.

